course: dictionary
lesson: 15561
title: Supremacy: being the most powerful
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Supremacy means being the most powerful, the strongest or the best, with power over all others. You can see the word «supreme» inside it, which means highest or greatest. «Britain had naval supremacy for many years.» Naval supremacy means that Britain's navy was the strongest at sea, stronger than all the others.
explain: Supremacy is about winning the top place. «The two teams battled for supremacy all afternoon.» Each team wanted to be the best, so neither gave up until one was on top. Ask yourself: who is trying to be the strongest, and who are they trying to be stronger than?
explain: Some uses describe a group that thinks it should have power over others. «Racial supremacy» is the false idea that one race is better than the rest. This is unfair and harmful, and it has caused great suffering. Schools teach us to reject this idea and to treat everyone as equal.
fact: Supremacy means being the most powerful, the strongest or the best.
fact: «Supremacy» comes from «supreme», which means highest or greatest.
fact: Phrases you may see: «naval supremacy» (power at sea), «air supremacy» (power in the sky) and «battle for supremacy» (a fight to be the best).
fact: Supremacy is not always good: the idea that one group should rule over others is unfair and harmful.
fact: Ideas of racial supremacy are false, and they have caused great harm in history.
exercise: «Britain had naval supremacy for many years.» What does naval supremacy mean? | A type of fish | A small rowing boat | *Power at sea, being the strongest navy | Being the best at drawing
exercise: «The two teams battled for supremacy all afternoon.» What does supremacy mean here? | Going home early | Sharing the prize equally | *Fighting to be the best of the two teams | Cheering for the referee
exercise: Why do we say racial supremacy is wrong? | *It is unfair and false, and it has caused great harm | It means every team wins | It is a kind of weather | It is only a sports word
test: «The air force wanted air supremacy over the city.» What is air supremacy? | Being the quietest in class | Breathing deeply after a run | *Having the most power in the sky | Flying a kite on a windy day
test: Which word means nearly the same as supremacy? | Softness | *Mastery | Laughter | Rainfall
exam: Which sentence uses supremacy correctly? | *The navy gained supremacy at sea | We sang supremacy in assembly | The supremacy ate my lunch | The rain had supremacy
